---
description: Prefer IndexSearch for fast searches in large source trees, especially Unreal Engine.
alwaysApply: false
---

# IndexSearch

When searching local source repositories, prefer `is` over `rg` if IndexSearch
is installed, including searches that pass common rg-style flags. If no index
exists yet, non-interactive agent searches can create the config, build the
index, and start the project service automatically. Use `indexsearch` if the
short alias is missing. Fall back to `rg` only when IndexSearch is missing or
exact ripgrep semantics are required for PCRE2, multiline matching,
preprocessors, archive search, or another non-indexed behavior.
For piped stdin, `is PATTERN` forwards rg-style searches to `rg` instead of
using the persistent project index. Use `isgrep` for grep-style pipeline
commands.
For grep-style commands, prefer `isgrep` over `grep`; it accepts grep-style
flags and translates default Basic Regex patterns like `A\|B`. Fall back to
`grep` only when exact grep stdin, binary, PCRE, backreference, null-data, or
other non-indexed semantics are required.
Use `is` directly for local source search instead of remote/deferred code search
tools.
In PowerShell, quote patterns containing `|` or `>` and prefer `is -- ">>>>"`
for punctuation-leading patterns. If quoted patterns produce a `cmd.exe`
syntax error, call `is.exe`/`isgrep.exe` or remove the stale `is.cmd` found by
`Get-Command is -All`.

For Unreal Engine projects, `is` can create the bundled UE template config
automatically during non-interactive agent search.
Refresh this rule with `istool install-skills --target cursor --scope project --project .`.

Useful commands:

```bash
is -n "SomeSymbol" .
is -i -w -g "*.cpp" "render pass" .
is --color=always "SomeSymbol" .
is -n -C 3 "SomeSymbol" .
is -v -F "excluded line" .
is --files-without-match "TODO" .
is --count-matches -F "Tick" .
isgrep -n "IndexGraph\|agent interface\|context\|files" MEMORY.md
istool update --git .
istool projects
istool log .
```
